# Desktop build configuration. Copy to `desktop/.env` (gitignored) and set your
# real backend origin. It is the ONLY place the backend hostname lives, so
# committed source carries no infrastructure details.
#
# At build time this single value becomes both of:
#   * VITE_API_BASE   — baked into apiBase.js so the bundled app's /api requests
#     resolve to the tailnet backend at runtime, and
#   * the CSP connect-src that pins fetch/SSE to exactly that origin.
#
# The app is fully bundled and never navigates to a remote origin, so no remote
# capability or Rust origin injection is involved — only JSON crosses the wire.
#
# An explicit `CC_DESKTOP_API_BASE=... npm run build` overrides this file.
#
# Your Tailscale backend (tailnet-only HTTPS), e.g.:
CC_DESKTOP_API_BASE=https://host.your-tailnet.ts.net:8443
